    "verified": [
      "The Pentax ME-F, using focus sensors in the camera body coupled with a motorised lens, became the first autofocus 35 mm SLR in 1981 (en.wikipedia, Autofocus).",
      "Lineage: Konica C35 AF (1977, first mass-produced AF camera) and Polaroid SX-70 Sonar (1978, first AF SLR) preceded it; the ME-F moved AF into the interchangeable-lens SLR."
    ],
